WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:04.114
Stage thirteen: new ways in.

2
00:00:05.100 --> 00:00:12.166
Camille switches watches: Strava becomes a third data source, instead of Garmin, never on top of it.

3
00:00:12.266 --> 00:00:17.412
One choice at install time, and anyone staying on Garmin sees no change.

4
00:00:18.262 --> 00:00:22.160
The coach reads the per-second streams of every run,

5
00:00:22.260 --> 00:00:30.742
and computes the same indicators as with a FIT file: zones, adjusted pace, decoupling, durability, energy.

6
00:00:31.592 --> 00:00:36.882
Let's be honest: no HRV, no sleep, no readiness.

7
00:00:36.982 --> 00:00:42.872
The morning check says “unavailable, Strava source”, and the coach simulates nothing.

8
00:00:43.722 --> 00:00:49.852
Under the morning summary, a Telegram bot: session done, perceived effort, pain.

9
00:00:49.952 --> 00:00:56.298
An RPE of seven, and the file is written, with no model and no API key.

10
00:00:57.148 --> 00:01:03.902
A pain of seven out of ten triggers the same advice to see a professional as /log.

11
00:01:04.002 --> 00:01:09.628
Strict allow list, and let's be clear: Telegram can read these messages.

12
00:01:10.478 --> 00:01:17.928
Two options, both off by default. First, the menstrual cycle: until you turn it on, no mention.

13
00:01:18.028 --> 00:01:25.382
Once on, it is context next to a low HRV, never a rule: a red verdict stays red.

14
00:01:26.232 --> 00:01:30.682
Next, the intake declared with /log can go to Garmin.

15
00:01:30.782 --> 00:01:36.336
The coach proposes, waits for an explicit yes, and writes one step at a time.

16
00:01:38.732 --> 00:01:41.910
Each door has its page in the documentation.

17
00:01:48.432 --> 00:01:52.930
To go further: the “Strava setup” page of the documentation.
